# Backend standards (DDD + CQRS + TDD)

Apply on Laravel under `index/`. Prefer **new** work in `index/modules/`. Do **not** mass-migrate `app/Domains/` or legacy controllers unless the user asks.

## TDD first (required)

1. Write a failing unit or feature test.
2. Implement the minimum code to pass.
3. Refactor while tests stay green.

Do not implement a new command, query, endpoint, or domain rule without a test in the same change.

## Architecture — modules (inward only)

```
Presentation / API → Application → Domain
Infrastructure → Domain
```

```text
modules/<Module>/
  Domain/                 # entities, VOs, ports, domain errors
  Application/
    Query/                # read DTOs implementing Shared Query
    Command/              # write DTOs implementing Shared Command
    Handler/              # QueryHandler / CommandHandler
  Infrastructure/         # Eloquent repos, HTTP, FS, queue adapters
  Presentation/           # Http/Controllers, Console, Jobs (thin)
  <Module>ServiceProvider.php

modules/Shared/
  Application/            # Query, QueryHandler, Command, CommandHandler, bus contracts
```

Namespace: `Modules\<Module>\...` via Composer (`"Modules\\": "modules/"`).

- **Domain**: no HTTP, Eloquent, Laravel facades, or I/O.
- **Application**: orchestration only. Depend on **ports**, never concrete adapters.
- **Infrastructure**: only layer that talks to the outside; implements Domain ports.
- **Presentation**: thin. Dispatch the bus; never new handlers or run Eloquent queries.
- Wire bindings in the module `ServiceProvider` (composition root).

Cross-module contracts live in `Modules\Shared`, not duplicated inside a feature module.

## CQRS

- **Command** = mutate. Data-only DTO (no deps in the constructor).
- **Query** = read. Must not load aggregates for writes or mutate domain state.
- Handler constructor = ports; `handle(Query|Command $msg)`.
- Controllers call the bus (`dispatch` / `ask`), not handlers directly.

```text
✅ Controller → bus → GetArticleListHandler(ports)
❌ Controller → Eloquent / Handler injected and called as a service
❌ Query/Command holding Eloquent or HttpClient
```

## No magic values

- Named constants / enums / value objects for statuses, roles, paths, error codes.
- No scattered string literals (`"running"`, `"prod"`) in domain or handlers.
- Reject path traversal (`..`); keep allowlists in one place.

## Testing

| Layer | Test type | Location |
|----|-----|----|
| Domain, handlers | Unit + Fake ports | `index/tests/Unit/Modules/<Module>/...` |
| HTTP, jobs, CLI | Feature / integration | `index/tests/Feature/Modules/<Module>/...` |

- Mirror `modules/<Module>/` under `tests/Unit/Modules/` or `tests/Feature/Modules/`.
- Never colocate tests next to production source.
- No live cluster / GitHub / production DB for unit tests.
- Every new endpoint, command, query, or invariant needs tests.

## Forbidden

- Business logic in controllers or route closures
- Domain / Application importing Laravel HTTP, Eloquent, or shell for external I/O
- Swallowing infra errors into fake “success”
- Query handlers mutating state
- Skipping tests for “simple” changes
- Mass-moving `app/Http` or `app/Domains` into `modules/` without an explicit request
